			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement advanced synchronization service and enhance configuration resilience\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive `SynchronizationService` in Cocoon, designed to handle real-time document synchronization with the Mountain backend via Tauri IPC. The service provides advanced features including conflict resolution strategies, performance monitoring, and robust error recovery with circuit breaker logic, aligning with Land's declarative effects-based architecture.\n\nThe `ConfigurationService` is updated to use new Tauri commands (`get_configuration_data`, `save_configuration_data`) for improved integration with Mountain, and adds conflict handling with exponential backoff retry logic. This ensures that configuration changes are reliably persisted even in the face of synchronization conflicts, enhancing the overall stability of the Cocoon extension host.\n\nTogether, these changes strengthen the core synchronization and configuration management capabilities of Cocoon, crucial for maintaining a consistent state between the extension host and the Mountain backend in the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "02d6385f01a4aa396eb260f92423ebcbf6071a89"
		},
